values ('bbbb0004-0000-4000-8000-00000000003b', 'en', null, 'Modern Physics: Relativity & Quantum', 'Modern physics is the physics that emerged after about 1900, when relativity and quantum theory overturned the older Newtonian picture of a clockwork universe. This course walks through special and general relativity, the quantum revolution, atomic and nuclear structure, and a short tour of the standard model, explaining the mathematics in plain words and writing every formula in simple text such as E=mc^2. Structure adapted from the Modern physics article on Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia (CC BY-SA 4.0).', null, 'foundations', 57, true, 'science', '{}')
